.TH SSMCP 1 "2026-11-16" "ssmcp 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ssmcp \- expose a local shell or coding agent through an SSH-authenticated MCP gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssmcp
.RB [ \-t " shell|codex|cc|pi|opencode" ]
.RB [ \-\-name " name" ]
.RB [ \-F " ssh_config" ]
.RB [ \-i " identity" ]
.RB [ \-p " port" ]
.RB [ \-\-shell " path" ]
.RB [ \-\-backend " program" ]
.I [user@]host
.RB [ \-\- " backend_args..." ]
.PP
.B ssmcp
.RB [ \-t " type" ]
.RB [ \-\-backend " program" ]
.B \-\-list-tools
.RB [ \-\- " backend_args..." ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ssmcp authenticates to OpenSSH using a public key and starts a local shell or
coding-agent backend. Multiple clients may connect under the same SSH account.
The server assigns each connection a random client ID and returns the account's
HTTPS MCP URL and a one-time OAuth login code.
.PP
One JSON object containing url, login_code, login_expires_in, client_id, name,
type, hostname and cwd is written to standard output. Live activity and
diagnostics use standard error. The cwd field is the startup directory; it does
not track shell directory changes or the workspaces of native agent sessions.
.PP
The external MCP catalog contains exactly two tools: list and code_mode.
Use list to discover clients and their native capabilities. Use code_mode to
run JavaScript that calls a selected capability over SSH. Selecting a different
backend with \-t does not add external MCP tools.
.PP
Keep the program running while its backend is in use. Ctrl-C or SIGTERM closes
the SSH connection, stops its backend and revokes OAuth grants associated with
that connection. Other clients under the account remain separately connected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " type"
.TQ
.BI \-\-type " type"
Select shell, codex, cc, pi or opencode. The default is shell.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
Set the client display name. The default combines hostname, backend type and
process ID. Names are limited to 128 UTF-8 bytes and may not contain control
characters or consist only of whitespace. Duplicate names are allowed; use the
server-generated client ID to select an unambiguous target.
.TP
.BI \-F " file"
Use a separate OpenSSH client configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-i " file"
Use the specified private key. ssh-agent is also supported.
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
Connect to the specified SSH port.
.TP
.BI \-\-shell " path"
Run the specified absolute shell path in a local pseudo-terminal. Valid only
with shell mode. The default is the absolute path in SHELL, or /bin/sh.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " program"
Override the native executable used by an agent backend. Not valid in shell mode.
.TP
.B \-\-list-tools
Start the local backend, discover its native capabilities, print a JSON catalog
and shut it down. Does not connect to SSH and does not accept user@host. This is
the native capability catalog, not the two-tool external MCP catalog.
.TP
.B \-\-
Pass remaining arguments to the selected agent executable without an additional
shell. Shell mode does not accept these arguments. Transport settings managed
by ssmcp must not be overridden.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH MCP TOOLS
.TP
.B list
With no arguments, return online client IDs, names, backend types, hostnames and
startup directories for the authenticated SSH account. With client_id, return
that client's native tool names, descriptions and schemas. Pass a returned
nextCursor as cursor to read another capability page.
.TP
.B code_mode
Accept a code string and optional timeout_ms. JavaScript has clients (a metadata
snapshot), await call(clientId, toolName, arguments), await tools(clientId,
cursor), print, console.log and top-level return. Calls return complete native
MCP results, including isError and structuredContent. Inspect isError even when
the JavaScript promise resolves. The code-mode structuredContent has result
(the script return value) and logs (an array of strings).
.PP
The server starts a system-installed Node.js process inside bubblewrap for each
request. Node.js 18 or newer and bubblewrap 0.8 or newer are server dependencies
managed by the operating system package manager; no npm package is needed. A client-only
ssmcp installation does not require these server dependencies. The public
JavaScript API is clients, call, tools and logging. Native backend calls execute
on the selected client with that local user's permissions. Runtime state is
fresh for each request; backend sessions remain alive.
.PP
The bridge script is installed at PREFIX/libexec/ssmcp/code-mode.js, normally
/usr/local/libexec/ssmcp/code-mode.js. The server environment variable
SSMCP_CODE_MODE_RUNNER may select an absolute script path. Missing dependencies
or unavailable namespace isolation cause code_mode to fail; list remains usable.
.PP
Timeout stops orchestration, but an already-started native action may continue.
Inspect native state before retrying a mutating action. Retain output cursors
and agent session IDs in the calling application for subsequent requests.
.SH BACKENDS
.TP
.B shell
An interactive local shell and PTY. Internal capabilities are terminal.read,
terminal.write, terminal.resize and terminal.status.
.TP
.B codex
Codex App Server over stdio. Requires schema generation support. The installed
CLI's generated client methods, events and approval responses are callable.
.TP
.B cc
Claude Code's native claude mcp serve entry point. Tools are discovered and
prefixed with cc.; their schemas and results are preserved. Native MCP tool
calls do not imply the interactive terminal's confirmation behavior.
.TP
.B pi
Pi's native JSONL RPC interface. Control commands use pi.; pi.rpc forwards
additional commands supported by the installed CLI. Events and extension
dialogs retain explicit read and response capabilities.
.TP
.B opencode
OpenCode v2 serve with a private loopback listener, stdio ready handshake and
OpenAPI discovery. Requires the v2 entry point; v1 is not supported. HTTP,
SSE and WebSocket capabilities use the same code-mode interface.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Only SSH public-key authentication is permitted. Standard OpenSSH host-key
verification remains enabled. Add the returned URL to an OAuth-capable MCP
client, then enter login_code on its authorization page. The client completes
Authorization Code with S256 PKCE and uses an access token as its Bearer
credential. The login code cannot be used as a Bearer token.
.PP
The destination may be a Host alias from ~/.ssh/config. OpenSSH resolves its
HostName, User, Port, IdentityFile, IdentityAgent and ProxyJump settings. An
explicit user@host overrides the configured User. Use \-F for a separate
configuration. Local ssh-agent authentication works without agent forwarding;
ssmcp disables forwarding, connection multiplexing and remote TTY allocation.
.PP
Public keys are managed by the server's OpenSSH authorized_keys policy. A key
already accepted for that account can be reused. On a ForceCommand-restricted
ssmcp account, update authorized_keys through a separate administrator account
or server console; ssh-copy-id and SFTP cannot execute their normal operations
through the fixed bridge command. Append the new public key, test a second
connection, then remove only the old key. Removing a key affects new SSH
authentication; close an existing connection to revoke its OAuth grants.
.PP
The login code expires 600 seconds after issue and is consumed by one successful
authorization. login_expires_in subtracts backend startup time. Access tokens
last at most one hour. Clients registered for the refresh_token grant receive
rotating refresh tokens; an authorization family lasts at most 24 hours.
.PP
An OAuth grant authorizes all current and subsequently attached clients under
the same SSH account while its source connection is live. Disconnecting that
source revokes its access and refresh tokens even if other clients remain
connected. Reconnect to obtain a new login code when a fresh authorization is
needed. Other SSH accounts are isolated.
.PP
Reopening an MCP application can reuse its saved, valid OAuth tokens while the
source SSH connection remains alive. Restarting ssmcp or ssmcpd requires a new
authorization. Expired, revoked or replayed refresh tokens produce invalid_grant;
reconnect with a fresh login code and authorize again. If a restarted server no
longer recognizes a cached client_id, register the MCP connection again.
.PP
Native agent permissions, request IDs and approval responses remain explicit.
ssmcp does not automatically answer native requests. Install and configure the
selected agent on the client; the gateway does not need that agent installed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ssmcp --name build-shell user@host
ssmcp --name build-shell my-server
ssmcp -t codex --name review-codex user@host
ssmcp -t cc --list-tools
.fi
.PP
Example JavaScript supplied as code_mode's code argument, using an ID from list:
.nf
return await call("CLIENT_ID_FROM_LIST", "terminal.status", {});
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
Default OpenSSH client configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/known_hosts
Trusted SSH host keys.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssmcpd (8),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
